{"$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/guitaripod/wwdc-sessions/master/schema/transcript.schema.json", "id": "wwdc2019-717", "language": "eng", "source": "https://developer.apple.com/videos/play/wwdc2019/717", "wordCount": 2840, "segments": [{"start": 7.0, "text": "Welcome to our session on"}, {"start": 8.0, "text": "Universal Links."}, {"start": 10.0, "text": "My name is Jonathan Grynspan and"}, {"start": 11.0, "text": "I work on the Core Frameworks"}, {"start": 13.0, "text": "Team at Apple."}, {"start": 14.0, "text": "Today, I'll be showing you how"}, {"start": 16.0, "text": "to use universal links in your"}, {"start": 18.0, "text": "app."}, {"start": 19.0, "text": "We introduced the universal"}, {"start": 20.0, "text": "links in iOS 9 as a great way to"}, {"start": 22.0, "text": "provide rich content both on the"}, {"start": 24.0, "text": "web and in your app."}, {"start": 26.0, "text": "Today, I'll be showing you the"}, {"start": 27.0, "text": "enhancements we've made to this"}, {"start": 29.0, "text": "feature."}, {"start": 30.0, "text": "Whether you've already adopted"}, {"start": 31.0, "text": "universal links in your iOS app"}, {"start": 33.0, "text": "or you're adding them to your"}, {"start": 34.0, "text": "macOS app, you will want to pay"}, {"start": 36.0, "text": "close attention to the changes"}, {"start": 37.0, "text": "I'll be discussing."}, {"start": 40.0, "text": "To begin, let's talk about what"}, {"start": 42.0, "text": "universal links are."}, {"start": 45.0, "text": "Universal links are HTTP or"}, {"start": 47.0, "text": "HTTPS URLs that Apple's"}, {"start": 50.0, "text": "operating systems recognize as"}, {"start": 52.0, "text": "pointing to resources either on"}, {"start": 54.0, "text": "the web or in your app."}, {"start": 56.0, "text": "This means that a single URL can"}, {"start": 58.0, "text": "represent that content, whether"}, {"start": 60.0, "text": "your users have your app"}, {"start": 61.0, "text": "installed or it just haven't"}, {"start": 63.0, "text": "downloaded it yet."}, {"start": 64.0, "text": "They are great way to increase"}, {"start": 65.0, "text": "user engagement within your app."}, {"start": 68.0, "text": "Universal links are introduced"}, {"start": 69.0, "text": "in iOS 9 and tvOS 10."}, {"start": 72.0, "text": "I'm happy to announce that we"}, {"start": 73.0, "text": "are introducing them to the Mac"}, {"start": 75.0, "text": "with macOS 10.15, whether you're"}, {"start": 77.0, "text": "using AppKit or UIKit."}, {"start": 80.0, "text": "I'll tell you more about that in"}, {"start": 81.0, "text": "a moment."}, {"start": 83.0, "text": "Universal links are securely"}, {"start": 84.0, "text": "associated between your app and"}, {"start": 86.0, "text": "your website."}, {"start": 87.0, "text": "Your app adopts an entitlement"}, {"start": 89.0, "text": "in Xcode that indicates which"}, {"start": 90.0, "text": "domains it can represent and"}, {"start": 92.0, "text": "your web server adopts a single"}, {"start": 94.0, "text": "JSON file that contains more"}, {"start": 96.0, "text": "details about what parts of its"}, {"start": 97.0, "text": "domain are representable in your"}, {"start": 99.0, "text": "app."}, {"start": 100.0, "text": "These two ways secure handshake"}, {"start": 102.0, "text": "ensures nobody can redirect your"}, {"start": 103.0, "text": "users into their apps instead of"}, {"start": 105.0, "text": "yours."}, {"start": 107.0, "text": "We recommend that where you are"}, {"start": 108.0, "text": "currently using custom URL"}, {"start": 110.0, "text": "schemes, you begin migrating to"}, {"start": 112.0, "text": "universal links today."}, {"start": 114.0, "text": "Custom URL schemes are"}, {"start": 115.0, "text": "inherently insecure and can be"}, {"start": 117.0, "text": "abused by malicious developers."}, {"start": 119.0, "text": "New uses of custom URL schemes"}, {"start": 121.0, "text": "are highly discouraged."}, {"start": 125.0, "text": "Now that we know what universal"}, {"start": 126.0, "text": "links are, let's talk about how"}, {"start": 128.0, "text": "to build them."}, {"start": 129.0, "text": "We'll start with your web"}, {"start": 130.0, "text": "server."}, {"start": 132.0, "text": "Your web server must have a"}, {"start": 134.0, "text": "valid HTTPS certificate."}, {"start": 137.0, "text": "HTTP is not secure and cannot be"}, {"start": 139.0, "text": "used to validate an association"}, {"start": 141.0, "text": "between your app and your"}, {"start": 143.0, "text": "website. The root certificate used to"}, {"start": 145.0, "text": "sign your HTTPS certificate must"}, {"start": 148.0, "text": "be recognized by the operating"}, {"start": 149.0, "text": "system."}, {"start": 150.0, "text": "Custom root certificates are not"}, {"start": 152.0, "text": "supported."}, {"start": 153.0, "text": "After generating your"}, {"start": 154.0, "text": "certificate and configuring your"}, {"start": 156.0, "text": "server, add your"}, {"start": 157.0, "text": "apple-app-site-association file."}, {"start": 160.0, "text": "This is a JSON file."}, {"start": 161.0, "text": "We'll discuss this format in a"}, {"start": 162.0, "text": "moment."}, {"start": 163.0, "text": "When your app is installed on an"}, {"start": 165.0, "text": "Apple device, the operating"}, {"start": 166.0, "text": "system downloads this file to"}, {"start": 168.0, "text": "determine what services the"}, {"start": 169.0, "text": "server will let your app use."}, {"start": 171.0, "text": "The system also periodically"}, {"start": 173.0, "text": "downloads updates for this file."}, {"start": 176.0, "text": "Universal links are one of many"}, {"start": 177.0, "text": "services that may be included in"}, {"start": 179.0, "text": "this file."}, {"start": 180.0, "text": "This file should be located at"}, {"start": 182.0, "text": "HTTPS://your domain name/"}, {"start": 187.0, "text": ".well-known/apple-app-site-"}, {"start": 190.0, "text": "association."}, {"start": 191.0, "text": "Other paths are deprecated."}, {"start": 194.0, "text": "In the past, we've discussed"}, {"start": 195.0, "text": "signing your"}, {"start": 196.0, "text": "apple-app-site-association file."}, {"start": 198.0, "text": "This has never been a necessary"}, {"start": 199.0, "text": "step to support universal links"}, {"start": 201.0, "text": "so it is now deprecated."}, {"start": 203.0, "text": "Support for sign JSON files and"}, {"start": 205.0, "text": "JSON files at other paths will"}, {"start": 207.0, "text": "be removed in a future release."}, {"start": 209.0, "text": "With that out of the way, let's"}, {"start": 212.0, "text": "take a look at your"}, {"start": 213.0, "text": "apple-app-site-association file."}, {"start": 216.0, "text": "If you already have one of these"}, {"start": 217.0, "text": "files on your web server this"}, {"start": 218.0, "text": "probably looks familiar, but we"}, {"start": 221.0, "text": "have a few changes to introduce"}, {"start": 222.0, "text": "today."}, {"start": 223.0, "text": "At the top level is a dictionary"}, {"start": 225.0, "text": "whose keys are service types."}, {"start": 227.0, "text": "For universal links, the key is"}, {"start": 228.0, "text": "applinks like you see here but"}, {"start": 230.0, "text": "other services are also"}, {"start": 232.0, "text": "available."}, {"start": 233.0, "text": "We'll be focusing solely on"}, {"start": 234.0, "text": "Universal Links."}, {"start": 236.0, "text": "Under that top level key are the"}, {"start": 238.0, "text": "apps key and the details key."}, {"start": 240.0, "text": "If you are targeting iOS 13,"}, {"start": 242.0, "text": "tvOS 13 and macOS 10.15, you do"}, {"start": 245.0, "text": "not need the apps key, so you"}, {"start": 247.0, "text": "can remove it."}, {"start": 249.0, "text": "If you are continuing to provide"}, {"start": 250.0, "text": "support for iOS 12, tvOS 12 or"}, {"start": 252.0, "text": "earlier, you'll still need it."}, {"start": 254.0, "text": "For universal links, it should"}, {"start": 256.0, "text": "always be an empty array."}, {"start": 258.0, "text": "The details key contains an"}, {"start": 260.0, "text": "array of dictionaries, each of"}, {"start": 261.0, "text": "which represents a specific apps"}, {"start": 263.0, "text": "universal links configuration."}, {"start": 265.0, "text": "In the past, we supported using"}, {"start": 267.0, "text": "a dictionary structure here"}, {"start": 268.0, "text": "instead of an array but that"}, {"start": 270.0, "text": "configuration is obsolete."}, {"start": 273.0, "text": "Under the details key is an"}, {"start": 274.0, "text": "appID key whose value is your"}, {"start": 276.0, "text": "app identifier."}, {"start": 278.0, "text": "Your app identifier consists of"}, {"start": 279.0, "text": "an alphanumeric, 10 character"}, {"start": 281.0, "text": "prefix provided by Apple, a"}, {"start": 283.0, "text": "period, and your bundle"}, {"start": 284.0, "text": "identifier."}, {"start": 286.0, "text": "The prefix may or may not be"}, {"start": 288.0, "text": "equal to your team identifier."}, {"start": 290.0, "text": "Check the developer portal to"}, {"start": 291.0, "text": "confirm your app identifier."}, {"start": 292.0, "text": "If you have multiple apps with"}, {"start": 295.0, "text": "the same universal links"}, {"start": 296.0, "text": "configuration, you may not want"}, {"start": 298.0, "text": "to repeat the relevant JSON."}, {"start": 300.0, "text": "If you are targeting this year's"}, {"start": 301.0, "text": "releases, you can reduce the"}, {"start": 303.0, "text": "size of this file by using the"}, {"start": 304.0, "text": "plural appIDs key."}, {"start": 306.0, "text": "The value of that key is an"}, {"start": 308.0, "text": "array of app identifiers."}, {"start": 310.0, "text": "If you need to support previous"}, {"start": 311.0, "text": "releases, you should keep using"}, {"start": 313.0, "text": "the singular appID key for each"}, {"start": 315.0, "text": "app."}, {"start": 316.0, "text": "Next is the paths key."}, {"start": 318.0, "text": "This key contains an array of"}, {"start": 319.0, "text": "path patterns."}, {"start": 320.0, "text": "Pattern matching is performed"}, {"start": 322.0, "text": "the same way it is in terminal."}, {"start": 324.0, "text": "The asterisk is used to indicate"}, {"start": 325.0, "text": "multiple wildcard characters"}, {"start": 327.0, "text": "while the question mark matches"}, {"start": 328.0, "text": "just one character."}, {"start": 330.0, "text": "Beginning this year, we are"}, {"start": 331.0, "text": "replacing the paths key with the"}, {"start": 333.0, "text": "components key."}, {"start": 335.0, "text": "This key's value is an array of"}, {"start": 336.0, "text": "dictionaries, each of which"}, {"start": 338.0, "text": "contains zero or more URL"}, {"start": 340.0, "text": "components to pattern match"}, {"start": 341.0, "text": "against."}, {"start": 342.0, "text": "As before, you can match against"}, {"start": 344.0, "text": "the URL's path component whose"}, {"start": 345.0, "text": "key is the forward slash."}, {"start": 347.0, "text": "If you need to support previous"}, {"start": 349.0, "text": "releases, you can keep the paths"}, {"start": 350.0, "text": "key."}, {"start": 352.0, "text": "iOS 13, tvOS 13 and macOS 10.15"}, {"start": 355.0, "text": "will ignore it if the components"}, {"start": 357.0, "text": "key is present."}, {"start": 358.0, "text": "And now you can match against"}, {"start": 360.0, "text": "the URL's fragment component"}, {"start": 361.0, "text": "whose key is the hash mark and"}, {"start": 363.0, "text": "you can match the query"}, {"start": 364.0, "text": "component whose key is the"}, {"start": 365.0, "text": "question mark."}, {"start": 367.0, "text": "Now many, if not most URLs out"}, {"start": 369.0, "text": "there divide their query"}, {"start": 370.0, "text": "component up into key value"}, {"start": 372.0, "text": "pairs called query items."}, {"start": 373.0, "text": "For the query component, you can"}, {"start": 375.0, "text": "specify a dictionary instead of"}, {"start": 377.0, "text": "a string as its value and"}, {"start": 379.0, "text": "pattern match individual query"}, {"start": 380.0, "text": "items."}, {"start": 381.0, "text": "URLs may repeat query item names"}, {"start": 383.0, "text": "and the operating system will"}, {"start": 384.0, "text": "require that all instances of a"}, {"start": 386.0, "text": "given query item name match your"}, {"start": 388.0, "text": "pattern."}, {"start": 389.0, "text": "Query items with no value and"}, {"start": 391.0, "text": "absent query items are treated"}, {"start": 392.0, "text": "by the operating system as if"}, {"start": 394.0, "text": "they have a value equal to the"}, {"start": 395.0, "text": "empty string."}, {"start": 397.0, "text": "For a components dictionary to"}, {"start": 399.0, "text": "match a candidate URL, all the"}, {"start": 401.0, "text": "specified components must match."}, {"start": 403.0, "text": "If you don't specify a"}, {"start": 404.0, "text": "component, the operating"}, {"start": 405.0, "text": "system's default behavior is to"}, {"start": 407.0, "text": "simply ignore that component."}, {"start": 409.0, "text": "So if, for example, your app"}, {"start": 411.0, "text": "doesn't care about the fragment"}, {"start": 412.0, "text": "component of a URL, you don't"}, {"start": 414.0, "text": "need to specify it in this file."}, {"start": 416.0, "text": "You may have sections of your"}, {"start": 417.0, "text": "website that are not able to be"}, {"start": 419.0, "text": "represented in your app yet."}, {"start": 421.0, "text": "You can exclude such subsections"}, {"start": 423.0, "text": "by specifying the exclude key"}, {"start": 425.0, "text": "with a Boolean value of true."}, {"start": 427.0, "text": "This key has the same behavior"}, {"start": 428.0, "text": "as a not keyword that you used"}, {"start": 430.0, "text": "in the old paths key."}, {"start": 432.0, "text": "That key word is not supported"}, {"start": 433.0, "text": "when using the component's"}, {"start": 434.0, "text": "dictionary."}, {"start": 436.0, "text": "Here we have a few examples of"}, {"start": 438.0, "text": "URLs that we need to pattern"}, {"start": 439.0, "text": "match."}, {"start": 440.0, "text": "I'm working on a meal ordering"}, {"start": 442.0, "text": "app and I'm using universal"}, {"start": 443.0, "text": "links to bring users into my app"}, {"start": 445.0, "text": "from Safari."}, {"start": 446.0, "text": "On the left, you can see some"}, {"start": 448.0, "text": "JSON from my server and on the"}, {"start": 450.0, "text": "right, you can see some URLs."}, {"start": 452.0, "text": "First, I want to match all the"}, {"start": 454.0, "text": "order forms on my website which"}, {"start": 456.0, "text": "are all located on a path where"}, {"start": 458.0, "text": "the first component can be"}, {"start": 459.0, "text": "anything."}, {"start": 460.0, "text": "The second component is order"}, {"start": 462.0, "text": "and there are no further path"}, {"start": 463.0, "text": "components afterward."}, {"start": 465.0, "text": "This pattern will match a URL"}, {"start": 467.0, "text": "such as these two on the right."}, {"start": 469.0, "text": "Time for lunch."}, {"start": 471.0, "text": "Next, I know a lot of my"}, {"start": 472.0, "text": "customers are going to want to"}, {"start": 474.0, "text": "put cheese on their tacos so I'm"}, {"start": 476.0, "text": "going to match any URL where the"}, {"start": 477.0, "text": "path starts with the path"}, {"start": 479.0, "text": "component taco and where a query"}, {"start": 481.0, "text": "item named cheese is specified."}, {"start": 484.0, "text": "You'll notice that I specify a"}, {"start": 485.0, "text": "question mark and an asterisk as"}, {"start": 487.0, "text": "the pattern from the query items"}, {"start": 489.0, "text": "value. A pattern consisting of a single"}, {"start": 492.0, "text": "asterisk matches any string,"}, {"start": 493.0, "text": "including the empty string."}, {"start": 495.0, "text": "And a missing query item has a"}, {"start": 496.0, "text": "value equivalent to the empty"}, {"start": 498.0, "text": "string."}, {"start": 499.0, "text": "So to match against the string"}, {"start": 500.0, "text": "that's at least one character"}, {"start": 502.0, "text": "long, I specify a question mark"}, {"start": 504.0, "text": "and then any additional"}, {"start": 505.0, "text": "characters are matched by the"}, {"start": 506.0, "text": "asterisk."}, {"start": 508.0, "text": "That matches our third URL."}, {"start": 511.0, "text": "The fourth and fifth URLs look"}, {"start": 513.0, "text": "very similar but there's a good"}, {"start": 515.0, "text": "reason for that."}, {"start": 516.0, "text": "My website also has lots of"}, {"start": 518.0, "text": "four-digit coupon codes that the"}, {"start": 519.0, "text": "app can handle."}, {"start": 520.0, "text": "But if they start with a 1, I"}, {"start": 523.0, "text": "want them to stay in the browser."}, {"start": 525.0, "text": "Because the operating system is"}, {"start": 526.0, "text": "going to look at the available"}, {"start": 527.0, "text": "patterns from top to bottom,"}, {"start": 529.0, "text": "we'll first mark coupon code"}, {"start": 531.0, "text": "starting with the one as"}, {"start": 532.0, "text": "excluded."}, {"start": 534.0, "text": "This tells the system to stop"}, {"start": 535.0, "text": "looking here if it finds a match"}, {"start": 537.0, "text": "but not to open the URL as a"}, {"start": 539.0, "text": "universal link."}, {"start": 540.0, "text": "Then any other coupon will match"}, {"start": 542.0, "text": "the fourth and final components"}, {"start": 544.0, "text": "dictionary."}, {"start": 548.0, "text": "Before we move on to your app,"}, {"start": 549.0, "text": "let's discuss how to support an"}, {"start": 551.0, "text": "international audience."}, {"start": 553.0, "text": "URLs are always ASCII coded so"}, {"start": 555.0, "text": "component matching is done in"}, {"start": 557.0, "text": "ASCII as well."}, {"start": 558.0, "text": "If you need to match Unicode"}, {"start": 560.0, "text": "characters present and code them"}, {"start": 561.0, "text": "like you would in your URL."}, {"start": 563.0, "text": "Because components are present"}, {"start": 565.0, "text": "and coded, a Unicode character"}, {"start": 566.0, "text": "may be represented by more than"}, {"start": 568.0, "text": "one ASCII character, so keep"}, {"start": 570.0, "text": "that in mind when using the"}, {"start": 571.0, "text": "question mark in your patterns."}, {"start": 573.0, "text": "When you build your JSON, you"}, {"start": 575.0, "text": "may be tempted to provide"}, {"start": 576.0, "text": "country-specific patterns for"}, {"start": 577.0, "text": "every country you support."}, {"start": 579.0, "text": "This increases the size of your"}, {"start": 580.0, "text": "JSON significantly."}, {"start": 582.0, "text": "If your pattern-matching is"}, {"start": 583.0, "text": "consistent between countries,"}, {"start": 585.0, "text": "you can reduce the traffic to"}, {"start": 586.0, "text": "and from your server by"}, {"start": 587.0, "text": "simplifying you JSON."}, {"start": 589.0, "text": "For instance, if you separate"}, {"start": 590.0, "text": "your content by two-letter"}, {"start": 591.0, "text": "country code, you need to only"}, {"start": 593.0, "text": "specify two question marks where"}, {"start": 595.0, "text": "you are previously using those"}, {"start": 596.0, "text": "country codes."}, {"start": 597.0, "text": "Other more complex patterns like"}, {"start": 599.0, "text": "you see here can also be matched"}, {"start": 601.0, "text": "easily."}, {"start": 602.0, "text": "If you encounter a URL with an"}, {"start": 604.0, "text": "invalid country code or locale"}, {"start": 605.0, "text": "specific identifier, just treat"}, {"start": 607.0, "text": "it like the user's current"}, {"start": 608.0, "text": "locale."}, {"start": 610.0, "text": "Beginning in this release, the"}, {"start": 611.0, "text": "operating system will prioritize"}, {"start": 613.0, "text": "apple-app-site-association"}, {"start": 615.0, "text": "downloads based on where a user"}, {"start": 616.0, "text": "is most likely to browse."}, {"start": 618.0, "text": "We'll still download them all"}, {"start": 619.0, "text": "when an app is installed but at"}, {"start": 621.0, "text": "different priorities."}, {"start": 622.0, "text": "The top-level domains .com,"}, {"start": 624.0, "text": ".net, and .org, are high"}, {"start": 627.0, "text": "priority domains because they"}, {"start": 628.0, "text": "account for so much internet"}, {"start": 629.0, "text": "traffic worldwide."}, {"start": 631.0, "text": "Country code TLDs also known as"}, {"start": 633.0, "text": "ccTLDs and internationalized"}, {"start": 636.0, "text": "TLDs are also prioritized if"}, {"start": 638.0, "text": "they match the user's current"}, {"start": 639.0, "text": "locale settings."}, {"start": 640.0, "text": "For example, the average user in"}, {"start": 642.0, "text": "China is more likely to visit a"}, {"start": 643.0, "text": "domain under a Chinese ccTLD"}, {"start": 646.0, "text": "than under, for example, an"}, {"start": 647.0, "text": "Italian or Russian ccTLD."}, {"start": 652.0, "text": "So now your server is ready to"}, {"start": 653.0, "text": "support universal links."}, {"start": 655.0, "text": "Let's update your app."}, {"start": 658.0, "text": "Open your project in Xcode and"}, {"start": 660.0, "text": "navigate to your project"}, {"start": 661.0, "text": "settings."}, {"start": 662.0, "text": "Add the Associated Domains"}, {"start": 663.0, "text": "capability."}, {"start": 665.0, "text": "This adds a new entitlement to"}, {"start": 666.0, "text": "the selected target."}, {"start": 668.0, "text": "You can modify this entitlement"}, {"start": 669.0, "text": "directly from this view."}, {"start": 673.0, "text": "The value of this entitlement is"}, {"start": 675.0, "text": "an array of strings of the form"}, {"start": 676.0, "text": "service type: domain name."}, {"start": 678.0, "text": "For universal links, the service"}, {"start": 680.0, "text": "type is applinks like it was in"}, {"start": 682.0, "text": "your apple-app-site-association"}, {"start": 684.0, "text": "file."}, {"start": 685.0, "text": "The order of values in this"}, {"start": 686.0, "text": "array is ignored by the system."}, {"start": 689.0, "text": "Here, we declare that your app"}, {"start": 690.0, "text": "supports universal links for"}, {"start": 691.0, "text": "www.example.com."}, {"start": 694.0, "text": "When your app is then installed,"}, {"start": 696.0, "text": "the operating system will visit"}, {"start": 697.0, "text": "www.example.com looking for the"}, {"start": 700.0, "text": "apple-app-site-association file"}, {"start": 702.0, "text": "we just discussed."}, {"start": 704.0, "text": "If it's present and it contains"}, {"start": 705.0, "text": "information for these apps, app"}, {"start": 707.0, "text": "identifier, then the association"}, {"start": 708.0, "text": "is confirmed."}, {"start": 710.0, "text": "It's also possible to indicate"}, {"start": 711.0, "text": "wildcard support for subdomains"}, {"start": 713.0, "text": "of a given domain as shown here."}, {"start": 715.0, "text": "In this case, the operating"}, {"start": 716.0, "text": "system will visit example.com."}, {"start": 718.0, "text": "No www at this time."}, {"start": 722.0, "text": "Exact domains have higher"}, {"start": 723.0, "text": "priority during universal links"}, {"start": 724.0, "text": "look up than wildcard domains."}, {"start": 727.0, "text": "In this case, that means when"}, {"start": 728.0, "text": "the system opens a URL at"}, {"start": 729.0, "text": "www.example.com, it will try to"}, {"start": 733.0, "text": "match patterns from that domain"}, {"start": 734.0, "text": "before the ones it got from the"}, {"start": 736.0, "text": "parent domain."}, {"start": 737.0, "text": "Patterns from the parent domain"}, {"start": 739.0, "text": "will only be matched if no match"}, {"start": 740.0, "text": "was found at the fully qualified"}, {"start": 742.0, "text": "subdomain."}, {"start": 743.0, "text": "Finally, here's an example of an"}, {"start": 745.0, "text": "internationalized domain."}, {"start": 747.0, "text": "Since URLs are always ASCII,"}, {"start": 749.0, "text": "your internationalized domain"}, {"start": 750.0, "text": "names will need to be encoded"}, {"start": 752.0, "text": "using Punycode."}, {"start": 753.0, "text": "For more information on"}, {"start": 754.0, "text": "Punycode, see RFC 3492."}, {"start": 760.0, "text": "Now that your app declares"}, {"start": 761.0, "text": "support for certain domains,"}, {"start": 762.0, "text": "you'll need to actually parse"}, {"start": 764.0, "text": "the URLs as they come in."}, {"start": 766.0, "text": "Universal links are based on"}, {"start": 767.0, "text": "foundations and as user activity"}, {"start": 769.0, "text": "class and are handled by your"}, {"start": 770.0, "text": "app delegate."}, {"start": 772.0, "text": "You'll need a handler for"}, {"start": 773.0, "text": "incoming user activities."}, {"start": 775.0, "text": "If you already support hand-off"}, {"start": 776.0, "text": "or other similar technologies,"}, {"start": 778.0, "text": "you may already have this method"}, {"start": 779.0, "text": "in your app delegate."}, {"start": 781.0, "text": "This method returns a bool."}, {"start": 782.0, "text": "Return true if you could"}, {"start": 783.0, "text": "successfully open the user"}, {"start": 785.0, "text": "activity and false if you"}, {"start": 786.0, "text": "couldn't."}, {"start": 787.0, "text": "If you're using UI scene, then a"}, {"start": 789.0, "text": "similar delegate method is"}, {"start": 791.0, "text": "available."}, {"start": 792.0, "text": "If you're using AppKit, the"}, {"start": 793.0, "text": "signature of this method is"}, {"start": 794.0, "text": "almost identical."}, {"start": 795.0, "text": "Just replace UI with NS like you"}, {"start": 798.0, "text": "see here."}, {"start": 799.0, "text": "We'll use UI application for the"}, {"start": 800.0, "text": "remainder of this session."}, {"start": 803.0, "text": "Next, we'll check that the"}, {"start": 804.0, "text": "activityType is"}, {"start": 805.0, "text": "NSUserActivityTypeBrowsingWeb."}, {"start": 808.0, "text": "This helps distinguish universal"}, {"start": 810.0, "text": "links from other incoming user"}, {"start": 811.0, "text": "activities that your app may"}, {"start": 812.0, "text": "support."}, {"start": 813.0, "text": "Even if you don't support other"}, {"start": 815.0, "text": "activity types now, it's a good"}, {"start": 817.0, "text": "idea to check the activity type"}, {"start": 818.0, "text": "in case you need to support"}, {"start": 820.0, "text": "other types in the future."}, {"start": 821.0, "text": "The activity type looks good."}, {"start": 824.0, "text": "Let's grab the webpage URL from"}, {"start": 825.0, "text": "the user activity object."}, {"start": 827.0, "text": "This will never be nil for a"}, {"start": 828.0, "text": "universal link and let's build a"}, {"start": 831.0, "text": "URL components draft from the"}, {"start": 832.0, "text": "URL."}, {"start": 833.0, "text": "You should always parse URLs"}, {"start": 835.0, "text": "using URL components."}, {"start": 837.0, "text": "Using regular expressions or"}, {"start": 838.0, "text": "manually parsing a URL string"}, {"start": 840.0, "text": "may leave you vulnerable to"}, {"start": 841.0, "text": "security issues."}, {"start": 843.0, "text": "We're past the guard statement"}, {"start": 844.0, "text": "so let's examine the contents of"}, {"start": 846.0, "text": "the URL."}, {"start": 847.0, "text": "In this case I'm interested in"}, {"start": 849.0, "text": "the query items of the URL but"}, {"start": 850.0, "text": "you can use any of the URL's"}, {"start": 851.0, "text": "components to root activities at"}, {"start": 853.0, "text": "this point."}, {"start": 854.0, "text": "If you support universal links"}, {"start": 856.0, "text": "from multiple domains, don't"}, {"start": 857.0, "text": "forget to check the host"}, {"start": 858.0, "text": "component."}, {"start": 861.0, "text": "Our code is complete and our"}, {"start": 862.0, "text": "server is configured but there"}, {"start": 864.0, "text": "are few differences when using"}, {"start": 865.0, "text": "universal links on macOS."}, {"start": 868.0, "text": "Universal links open in the"}, {"start": 869.0, "text": "browser by default on macOS."}, {"start": 871.0, "text": "When they do, Safari will give"}, {"start": 872.0, "text": "the user the option to open them"}, {"start": 874.0, "text": "in your app."}, {"start": 875.0, "text": "If the user selects this option,"}, {"start": 877.0, "text": "your links will continue to open"}, {"start": 878.0, "text": "in your app afterward."}, {"start": 881.0, "text": "Unlike iOS, macOS supports"}, {"start": 883.0, "text": "launching apps present on remote"}, {"start": 884.0, "text": "volumes."}, {"start": 885.0, "text": "Apps on remote volumes cannot"}, {"start": 887.0, "text": "use universal links."}, {"start": 888.0, "text": "They must be installed locally."}, {"start": 890.0, "text": "If the user downloads your app"}, {"start": 892.0, "text": "from the App Store, the system"}, {"start": 894.0, "text": "will begin downloading"}, {"start": 895.0, "text": "apple-app-site-association files"}, {"start": 897.0, "text": "as soon as soon as your app is"}, {"start": 898.0, "text": "installed or updated."}, {"start": 900.0, "text": "If your app is developer"}, {"start": 901.0, "text": "ID-signed, the system will not"}, {"start": 902.0, "text": "begin these downloads until the"}, {"start": 903.0, "text": "user has launched your app at"}, {"start": 905.0, "text": "least once."}, {"start": 907.0, "text": "Because a universal link is"}, {"start": 908.0, "text": "backed by a secure association"}, {"start": 910.0, "text": "with an app identifier, only one"}, {"start": 912.0, "text": "copy of a given app will be able"}, {"start": 913.0, "text": "to handle universal links on a"}, {"start": 915.0, "text": "Mac."}, {"start": 916.0, "text": "Typically, this will be the copy"}, {"start": 917.0, "text": "of the app present in slash"}, {"start": 919.0, "text": "applications."}, {"start": 920.0, "text": "Keep that in mind anytime you"}, {"start": 921.0, "text": "need to test changes to your"}, {"start": 922.0, "text": "associated domains entitlement."}, {"start": 925.0, "text": "If you are on the other end of"}, {"start": 926.0, "text": "an operation and want to open a"}, {"start": 928.0, "text": "universal link, UIApplication"}, {"start": 930.0, "text": "and NSWorkspace and launch"}, {"start": 931.0, "text": "services will all automatically"}, {"start": 933.0, "text": "open them when available."}, {"start": 935.0, "text": "If you want to require opening a"}, {"start": 937.0, "text": "universal link in an app rather"}, {"start": 938.0, "text": "than the default browser, you"}, {"start": 940.0, "text": "can use UIApplication or"}, {"start": 942.0, "text": "NSWorkspace API as appropriate."}, {"start": 944.0, "text": "If these open operations fail,"}, {"start": 946.0, "text": "it means that a universal link"}, {"start": 947.0, "text": "was not available for the"}, {"start": 948.0, "text": "supplied URL."}, {"start": 950.0, "text": "If you're developing a web"}, {"start": 951.0, "text": "browser from macOS, additional"}, {"start": 953.0, "text": "API will be made available to"}, {"start": 955.0, "text": "help you support universal"}, {"start": 956.0, "text": "links."}, {"start": 958.0, "text": "To help you make the best apps"}, {"start": 960.0, "text": "and to provide the best user"}, {"start": 961.0, "text": "experience, I've got a few final"}, {"start": 963.0, "text": "tips to share with you."}, {"start": 965.0, "text": "The first is to fail gracefully."}, {"start": 968.0, "text": "It's possible you'll be provided"}, {"start": 969.0, "text": "with URLs that represent"}, {"start": 971.0, "text": "outdated, invalid, or"}, {"start": 972.0, "text": "nonexistent content."}, {"start": 974.0, "text": "If you determine that a"}, {"start": 975.0, "text": "universal link can't be opened"}, {"start": 976.0, "text": "by your app, you can often open"}, {"start": 978.0, "text": "it in Safari View Controller."}, {"start": 980.0, "text": "This keeps the user engaged in"}, {"start": 981.0, "text": "your app."}, {"start": 982.0, "text": "If Safari View Controller is not"}, {"start": 984.0, "text": "an option, consider opening the"}, {"start": 986.0, "text": "URL in Safari, or at a minimum,"}, {"start": 988.0, "text": "prompting with details about the"}, {"start": 989.0, "text": "issue."}, {"start": 990.0, "text": "Avoid sending the user to a"}, {"start": 991.0, "text": "blank screen."}, {"start": 993.0, "text": "If the user is visiting your"}, {"start": 995.0, "text": "website, use the Smart App"}, {"start": 997.0, "text": "Banner to provide a link either"}, {"start": 998.0, "text": "to the App Store or to your"}, {"start": 999.0, "text": "content."}, {"start": 1000.0, "text": "The Smart App Banner integrates"}, {"start": 1002.0, "text": "seamlessly with Safari and looks"}, {"start": 1003.0, "text": "great."}, {"start": 1004.0, "text": "And there's no JavaScript or"}, {"start": 1005.0, "text": "custom URL schemes required to"}, {"start": 1007.0, "text": "support it."}, {"start": 1008.0, "text": "Finally, if you have feedback on"}, {"start": 1010.0, "text": "how we can improve universal"}, {"start": 1011.0, "text": "links, I would love to hear it."}, {"start": 1013.0, "text": "Please use the feedback"}, {"start": 1014.0, "text": "assistant and let us know what"}, {"start": 1015.0, "text": "we can do to make universal"}, {"start": 1016.0, "text": "links even better."}]}
